# The violations of `glutter-gen errcheck` that SPEC §14.4 accepts (step 24.1). Each line is
# "rule file:Func" with the reason above it. A line that no longer matches a violation is an
# error, so the file cannot grow stale.
#
#   go run ./cmd/glutter-gen errcheck -allow cmd/glutter-gen/errcheck.allow

# error-helper (R4): vkError turns the VkResult of a Vulkan call into one of three tags with a
# switch (device lost, out of memory, any other failure) and about a dozen calls use it. The
# route of such an error has the frame vkError; inlining the switch at every call would repeat
# the table. The other converters (eglError) were inlined.
error-helper internal/gpu/vulkan/check.go:vkError

# error-helper (R4): hresultError turns the HRESULT of a method of the audio client into one of four tags with a switch (a format
# that is not taken, a microphone that is not allowed, a device that is gone, any other failure), like win32.HResultError does for the
# other COM calls; about fifteen calls of the WASAPI backend use it. The route of such an error has the frame hresultError; the
# switch is the table of the numbers of AUDCLNT_E_*, which inlined at each call would be repeated.
error-helper internal/platform/windows/wasapi/com_windows.go:hresultError

# error-helper (R4): resultError turns the result of a function of AAudio into one of three tags with a switch (a rate, a format or an
# argument that the device does not take; the loss of the device; any other failure), with the name of the function, the number and
# AAudio's own text as the metadata; about ten calls of the Android backend use it. The route of such an error has the frame
# resultError; the switch is the table of the numbers of AAUDIO_ERROR_*, which inlined at each call would be repeated.
error-helper internal/platform/android/aaudio/service.go:resultError

# error-rewrap (R3): aaudio.Permissions is an interface of this package that the platform implements over the link to the activity, so
# the error of RecordAudio (a prompt that no activity could show, a context that ended) is tagged with the link's names; what an app
# matches on is AudioCapturePermissionDenied (SPEC §28.3), and the link's error stays as the cause, so errors.Is still finds it.
error-rewrap internal/platform/android/aaudio/service.go:Service.Open

# error-rewrap (R3): the public tags of SPEC §14.1 (FileChooserUnavailable,
# NotificationsUnavailable, TrayUnavailable, TrayRegisterFailed) are what an app matches on
# when the portal or the service is missing. internal/dbus tags its failures first
# (DBusCallFailed, DBusSubscribeFailed); package desktop gives the service's tag when
# portalMissing says that nobody serves the interface, and the bus's error stays as the cause
# (OriginalErr), so errors.Is still finds it. Moving the public tags into internal/dbus would
# put the knowledge of every service there.
error-rewrap desktop/file_chooser.go:call.chooseFiles
error-rewrap desktop/notifications.go:CloseNotification
error-rewrap desktop/notifications.go:call.show
error-rewrap desktop/notifications.go:call.showWithPortal
error-rewrap desktop/notifications.go:services.followNotifications
error-rewrap desktop/tray.go:tray.register

# error-rewrap (R3): LocalizationsDelegate is an interface that the app implements, so the
# error of Load is not tagged by this module; the tag LocalizationsLoadFailed is the first one.
error-rewrap widgets/localizations.go:localizationsState.load

# error-rewrap (R3): services.AssetBundle is an interface that the app implements, so the error of
# Load is not always tagged by this module; SPEC §26.5 names one tag for an asset that cannot be
# read (SvgLoadFailed, with the "source"), and the bundle's error (AssetNotFound for Glutter's)
# stays as the cause, so errors.Is still finds it.
error-rewrap svg/loaders.go:assetSource.load

# error-rewrap (R3): SPEC §27.11 names two tags of package gpu that an app matches on: a read that
# failed is GPUReadFailed (Buffer.Read, with the explicit device's error as the cause) and a shader
# that the backend cannot compile is GPUShaderCompileFailed (the pipeline constructors). The
# explicit devices tag their failures first, with their own names (VulkanCallFailed,
# ShaderModuleInvalid, D3D12ShaderCompileFailed); the public API must not leak those. Device
# loss, memory and the pending device pass through untouched (passesBackendError).
error-rewrap gpu/buffer.go:Buffer.Read
error-rewrap gpu/pipeline.go:Device.NewRenderPipeline
error-rewrap gpu/pipeline.go:Device.NewComputePipeline

# error-untagged (R3): ctxReader is an io.Reader, and the readers around it compare what it returns with io.EOF
# (io.ReadFull, io.LimitReader, io.CopyN): a tagged error would hide the end of the file from them. The error of the
# context and the error of the reader go through as they are, and Decode tags what ends the read where it first appears.
error-untagged audio/wav/wav.go:ctxReader.Read
